  ],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "Now let's find a simpler way to perform the same rotation.",
      "start_ms": 0,
      "end_ms": 4500,
      "start_frame": 0,
      "end_frame": 135,
      "word_count": 11
    },
    {
      "text": "We already know the final coordinate mapping.",
      "start_ms": 5240,
      "end_ms": 8020,
      "start_frame": 157,
      "end_frame": 241,
      "word_count": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "A value at row R column C must end at row C column N minus 1 minus R.",
      "start_ms": 8720,
      "end_ms": 16500,
      "start_frame": 262,
      "end_frame": 495,
      "word_count": 18
    },
    {
      "text": "Instead of doing that complete movement directly, we can split it into two simple transformations.",
      "start_ms": 17040,
      "end_ms": 24060,
      "start_frame": 511,
      "end_frame": 722,
      "word_count": 15
    },
    {
      "text": "First, transpose the matrix, transpose swaps, rows and columns.",
      "start_ms": 24600,
      "end_ms": 29200,
      "start_frame": 738,
      "end_frame": 876,
      "word_count": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "So, R C becomes C R.",
      "start_ms": 29200,
      "end_ms": 33180,
      "start_frame": 876,
      "end_frame": 995,
      "word_count": 6
    },
    {
      "text": "Now notice, the row is already correct.",
      "start_ms": 33620,
      "end_ms": 35900,
      "start_frame": 1009,
      "end_frame": 1077,
      "word_count": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "We only need TING to fix the column.",
      "start_ms": 36220,
      "end_ms": 38360,
      "start_frame": 1087,
      "end_frame": 1151,
      "word_count": 8
    },
    {
      "text": "So the second step is reverse every row that changes column R into column N minus 1 minus R.",
      "start_ms": 39180,
      "end_ms": 46920,
      "start_frame": 1175,
      "end_frame": 1408,
      "word_count": 19
    },
    {
      "text": "So together, transpose changes R C into C R.",
      "start_ms": 47380,
      "end_ms": 52920,
      "start_frame": 1421,
      "end_frame": 1588,
      "word_count": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "And reversing the row changes it into C N minus 1 minus R, which is exactly the coordinate mapping for a 90 degree clockwise rotation.",
      "start_ms": 52920,
      "end_ms": 64720,
      "start_frame": 1588,
      "end_frame": 1942,
      "word_count": 25
    },
    {
      "text": "So our plan is simple.",
      "start_ms": 65500,
      "end_ms": 66700,
      "start_frame": 1965,
      "end_frame": 2001,
      "word_count": 5
    },
    {
      "text": "Step one, transpose the matrix.",
      "start_ms": 67180,
      "end_ms": 69080,
      "start_frame": 2015,
      "end_frame": 2072,
      "word_count": 5
    },
    {
      "text": "Step two, reverse every row.",
      "start_ms": 69660,
      "end_ms": 71920,
      "start_frame": 2090,
      "end_frame": 2158,
      "word_count": 5
    },
    {
      "text": "Now let's execute these two transformations on the full matrix.",
      "start_ms": 72680,
      "end_ms": 77500,
      "start_frame": 2180,
      "end_frame": 2325,
      "word_count": 10
    }
  ],
